Actual-pair control:


```text
(f,g) = (pi, pi - gamma^2/2)
J(f,g) = gamma
monic in pi: true
reciprocal Lemma-shape anchor degrees: (2,2)
target tuple classifier: FAIL
```

This confirms that the wrapper is not an always-empty machine and that the
tuple classifier does not absorb an actual Jacobian pair into the D <= 200
target rows.

