+## 6. Computations
+
+### 6.1 Ring and controls
+
+**MEASURED.** Executable cases use the charged `(d',e')=(2,3)` A/B system:
+`h=H_lambda+D1-lower terms`, `beta=bp*A+bq*y+br*x+bs`, monic division in `y`,
+and the h-adic equation `J(f,g)=c*x^k`. The declared rings are polynomial rings
+over `GF(p)` or `Q` in the `h` coefficients, slope parameters, four beta
+parameters, `c`, and `T`, with `dp` order.
+
+**MEASURED.** Each main ideal contains
+
+```text
+T*(c*Omega)-1.
+```
+
+In the identical declared ring, `<c*Omega,T*c*Omega-1>` reduces to `[1]`, while
+`<c*Omega-1,T*c*Omega-1>` does not. Both controls passed on every reported
+run. Monic division introduces no parameter-dependent leader.
+
+### 6.2 `(33,22;30;8;k=1)`
+
+**MEASURED.** These are all source-safe partitions because `deg q=3` permits
+at most two noncentre factors.
