+## 3. The safe general rule—and where it stops
+
+**DERIVED from Prop. 6.3 and the charged drop rule.** For an original skeleton
+with `u_s=1`, first form `n'=n/d_s`, `m'=m/d_s`, and
+`k=V_s-u_s-1=V_s-2`; divide retained `M` entries by `d_s`, remove any
+`M'=n'-1` level, and carry its surviving `V` path to `(M2',V2')`. The nine
+instances are checked explicitly in section 5. The original singleton
+`u_s=1` enables this descent; it is not a theorem that one of the later
+descended multiplicities `e_i` is one.
+
+Let the descended data be `(n',m';M2',V2';k)` and put
+
+```text
+K=d2'=gcd(n',m'),  u'=K-V2',  d'=m'/K,  e'=n'/K.
+```
+
+**DERIVED.** At final level `r=2`, Def. 5.1 has `V3=d3`; hence the common
+boundary polynomial `p` has degree `K`. The selected major factor accounts for
+`V2'`, so all other `p`-factor multiplicities form a partition
+`lambda=(e_1,...,e_l)` with `sum e_i=u'`.
+
+**DERIVED.** Proposition 4.6 gives `deg q=n'-M2'` at this level. Therefore
+
+```text
+1+l <= n'-M2'.
+```
+
+The extra `1` is the selected `V2'` factor. Its condition that `p` not be a
+power of `q` must also be retained; none of the 30 strata in section 5 violates
+it.
+
+**DERIVED, conditional on actual boundary data.** If the distinct noncentre
+residue constants are `a_i`, then
+
+```text
+H_lambda(x,y) = y^V2' product_i (y-a_i*x)^e_i,
+f_top = H_lambda^d',                 g_top = H_lambda^e'.
+```
+
+Thus the number of noncentre roots of `H` is exactly `u'` with multiplicity,
+while the corresponding root packets contain `d'e_i` roots of `f` and
+`e'e_i` roots of `g`. Distinct child discs separate at the known top radius
+`delta2'=-1`; radii and splits *inside* a repeated `e_i` block are not known.
+
+**DERIVED.** The monomial Jacobian marks the line `x=0`. Coordinate changes
+that retain `J=c*x^k` can put the selected major slope at zero and one nonzero
+slope at one, but they do not remove all remaining slopes. For
+`lambda=(e_1,...,e_l)` use the source-complete family
+
+```text
+H_V[e_1,...,e_l]
+ = y^V (y-x)^e_1 product_(i=2..l) (y-a_i*x)^e_i,
+
+Omega = product_(i>=2) a_i(a_i-1) product_(2<=i<j) (a_i-a_j) != 0.
+```
+
+There are `l-1` slope parameters. Fixing them numerically is a slice unless a
+separate source statement fixes them. The Singular charts saturate by
+`c*Omega`, not merely by `c`.
+
+**OPEN[INVERSE-MINOR].** Moh's one example says its inverse transformation
+forces a minor disc. If this were proved generally, at least one part would
+satisfy
+
+```text
+e_i <= floor(K/(n'-M2')).
+```
+
+That is an additional necessary condition, not a sourced theorem for all
+descendants. It selects 21 of the 30 source-safe overcases; it is never used to
+discard one of the other nine in this report.
+
